tatus="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANNO KAZUNOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WADA NARUHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOJIMA, MASAHARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, YUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANNO, KAZUNOBU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WADA, NARUHITO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A safe and high-performance method for detecting and assaying anti-GAD antibody which exhibits a high sensitivity and a high specificity comparable to those achieved by radioimmunoassay; and a kit therefor. The above method is characterized by bringing a specimen into contact with a support carrying a recombinant GAD antigen solid phase, thus bonding the antigen to the antibody contained in the specimen to thereby form a complex, and detecting the complex with the use of chemiluminescent dioxetane having a group which can be cleaved with an enzyme and an antibody labeled with an enzyme capable of cleaving the above group to thereby induce chemiluminescence.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une méthode sûre et très performante de détection et de dosage d'anticorps anti-GAD présentant une sensibilité et une spécificité élevées comparables à celles qu'on obtient par dosage radioimmunologique, et une trousse associée à ladite méthode. Cette méthode consiste à placer un prélèvement au contact d'un support comprenant une phase solide d'un antigène GAD recombinant, à lier l'antigène à l'anticorps présent dans le prélèvement pour former un complexe, puis à détecter le complexe au moyen d'un dioxetane chimiluminescent comportant un groupe clivable par une enzyme et un anticorps marqué par une enzyme capable de cliver ledit groupe pour induire une chimiluminescence.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>